<title>INDIA: India 96/97 soybean output seen at 5.11 mln tonnes.</title>
<headline>India 96/97 soybean output seen at 5.11 mln tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's soybean output in 1996/97 (July-June) is expected to rise to 5.11 million tonnes from 4.99 million in the same period in 1995/96, the government said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The government, in its annual Economic Survey, said groundnut output in 1996/97 was expected to be 9.12 million tonnes against 7.81 million in 1995/96.</p>
<p>India's total oilseeds output in 1996/97 was expected to be 24.11 million tonnes, of which winter output was expected to be 14.41 million and summer output 9.70 million.</p>
<p>India produced 22.43 million tonnes of oilseeds in 1995/96.</p>
<p>--New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
